{
  "opening": "This release addresses several critical correctness issues and introduces new utility functions to enhance the library's robustness. Please ensure all public APIs behave according to the specifications below, particularly regarding error handling and edge cases.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "When using funcutils.wraps, defaulted positional and keyword-only arguments from the wrapped function must be passed as keyword arguments to the wrapper, rather than positional arguments. Wrappers that previously relied on inspecting *args for these parameters must now inspect **kwargs."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "No observable behavior change is required for pathutils as this change only adds tests."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The Bits class must raise a ValueError if the provided value requires more bits than the specified length, ensuring that the internal bit representation strictly matches the declared length. Previously, values that exceeded the bit capacity were silently accepted, leading to incorrect round-tripping."
    },
    {
      "id": "m04",
      "text": "JSONLIterator must no longer hang when seeking past the last newline or with negative relative seeks; it should handle EOF boundaries correctly without blocking. MultiReplace must treat empty substitution maps as a no-op instead of raising KeyError. Table.to_text must render empty tables without crashing, omitting header rows when headers are None or short. isoparse must correctly parse fractional seconds up to six digits and truncate longer fractions rather than raising an error. daterange must raise ValueError for zero or self-cancelling steps and yield nothing for wrong-direction steps. xfrange must yield results for descending ranges, aligning its count-based semantics with frange at inexact float boundaries."
    },
    {
      "id": "m06",
      "text": "funcutils.update_wrapper and related functions must forward arguments that the target callable accepts only as keywords, even if the donor function accepts them positionally. This ensures that wrappers built by wraps do not raise TypeError when calling targets with keyword-only parameters."
    },
    {
      "id": "m08",
      "text": "No observable behavior change is required for setutils as this change only covers existing logic and removes redundant code checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "strutils.ellipsize must truncate text at word boundaries to fit within max_len, including the ellipsis, and raise ValueError if max_len is too short. It must preserve decimal points between digits and hard-cut single tokens exceeding the limit."
    },
    {
      "id": "m10",
      "text": "args2sh and args2cmd must use the provided sep argument to join or separate arguments, allowing callers to customize the separator string instead of being hardcoded to spaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "m11",
      "text": "Stats.mode must return the most common value in the data, supporting non-numeric categorical inputs, and resolve ties by returning the first occurring value. A module-level convenience function for mode must also be available."
    },
    {
      "id": "m12",
      "text": "urlutils.parse_qsl must respect the encoding parameter when decoding query string keys and values, passing it to unquote instead of defaulting to UTF-8 regardless of input."
    },
    {
      "id": "m13",
      "text": "OrderedMultiDict.addlist must correctly handle one-shot iterators by materializing their values before insertion, preventing internal inconsistency where keys exist but values are missing. Empty iterators must result in keys with no associated values, maintaining consistency between len, keys, and getlist."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "ecoutils.get_profile must skip identifying lookups during scrubbing operations to improve performance or avoid side effects, though the specific functional impact is internal to the scrubbing process."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please verify these behaviors against the updated documentation and test suites. Your prompt attention to these fixes will ensure a stable release for our users."
}
